   314	Aftercare typically includes follow-up appointments with your surgeon,
   315	ongoing dietitian and exercise physiology support, nutritional
   316	monitoring via blood tests, and guidance on building sustainable habits.
   317	It matters because surgery changes your body, but long-term results are
   318	shaped by what happens in the months and years that follow. Patients who
   319	stay engaged with their care team consistently tend to achieve better
   320	long-term outcomes. At Obesity Surgery WA, we view your surgery as the
   321	beginning of your weight loss journey, not the end.</span>
   322	
   323	<span class="mark">**6. Where will my surgery and appointments take
   324	place?  **
   325	Consultations take place at our clinics in Booragoon or Greenfields,
   326	with surgeries performed at [<u>Mount Private
   327	Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private
   328	Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private
   329	Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/) in Perth. Once your
   330	surgery is planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to
   331	expect, where to go, and who will be involved at every stage, so there
   332	are no surprises on the day.</span>
   333	
   334	<span class="mark">**7. I have had weight loss surgery before — can it
   335	be revised?  **
   336	Yes, revision surgery is available for patients whose previous procedure
   337	is no longer working as intended, has caused complications, or requires
   338	conversion to a different procedure. Common examples include removing or
   339	converting an older gastric band, or converting a sleeve to a bypass.
   340	Revision surgery is generally more complex than a primary procedure, and
   341	your surgeon will assess your history carefully before making any
   342	recommendation.</span>
