+> Bariatric surgery is generally considered suitable for adults with a BMI of 40 or higher, or in specific circumstances for those with a BMI of 35 or higher when an obesity-related health condition is also present. People with a BMI between 30 and 35 may be candidates in specific circumstances, particularly where type 2 diabetes is poorly controlled.
+
+> MBS eligibility is assessed individually. The relevant thresholds are BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major obesity-related comorbidity. A BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold; discuss any other clinical pathway with your surgeon.
