+### G5 — brief corrections applied
+
+The brief direction now:
+
+- Describes laparoscopic techniques without saying they “make these procedures safe for most suitable candidates,” and prohibits comparative safety, pain or recovery claims.
+- States the MBS rule as BMI 40+, or BMI 35+ with a major obesity-related comorbidity, assessed individually; BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold.
+- Avoids comparative weight-loss, “preferred” and outcome-assurance wording in the procedure bullets.
+- Uses conditional Medicare/private-health wording, requires any range or estimate to be discussed at consultation, and keeps dollar figures out.
+- Includes Perth cost, Medicare coverage, the 30/30 rule, who may not meet MBS or clinical suitability requirements, 10-year variation and how to assess a surgeon in the FAQ plan.
+- Marks the GLP-1/active-ingredient wording as pending TGA/legal review; if retained, use active-ingredient/class names only and no brand names.
+
+Verification flags: hospital identity and affiliations remain to be verified; the GLP-1/medical-weight-management advertising policy remains pending; confirm current MBS, referral and insurer details before publication.
+
+## Batch-1 completion report
